BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Build a prefix-free binary code with minimum weighted path length for symbols with known) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 665 Td (    frequencies.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 645 Td (GREEDY CHOICE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631 Td (Put all symbol frequencies in a min-priority queue. Repeatedly remove the two smallest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618 Td (    nodes and combine them into a parent with summed frequency.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 598 Td (ALGORITHM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (Insert each symbol as a leaf. While more than one node remains, merge the two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (    minimum-frequency nodes and reinsert the parent. The final tree defines the codes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 551 Td (EXAMPLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 537 Td (For frequencies A:5, B:9, C:12, D:13, E:16, F:45, low-frequency symbols are merged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (    first; frequent symbols usually get shorter codes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 504 Td (COMPLEXITY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 490 Td (For k symbols, using a binary min-heap takes O\(k log k\) time and O\(k\) space.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 470 Td (TAKEAWAY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 456 Td (A prefix-free code means no symbol's code is the prefix of another symbol's code.) Tj ET
